<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kuching</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kuching is the capital of Sarawak, Malaysia, on the Sarawak River in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a>. A small Malay trading settlement under Brunei, it became the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-brooke">James Brooke</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-raj">Raj</a> of Sarawak in 1841 and grew under the Brooke rajahs, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astana">Astana</a> palace and Fort Margherita stand on the river. Japanese forces occupied it from December 1941 to 1945, and it remained the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-colony">Crown Colony</a> of Sarawak and of the Malaysian state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kuching.jpg" alt="Kuching" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mike86 at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kuching_Skyline.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
